# Credential-durability test image: creddisk on a real-disk KRFFS.
#
# Built into a partitioned disk by mkdisk.sh and booted three times against one
# scratch copy with rach2.fsdisk + rach2.rescue. The first boot publishes both
# files, the second reads them back and clears the lock its cut-off writer left,
# the third reads back that release. Each file is staged root-owned at a mode the
# replacement must reproduce, the shape /etc/shadow carries; the two modes differ
# so the inheritance is read rather than assumed.
file 0755 /creddisk build/tests/musl/creddisk
text 0600 /credtarget original\n
text 0640 /credalso original\n

# The lock's directory, since the probe takes the transaction the shipped
# writers take, at the path compiled into the library.
dir 0755 /etc
